Z||000003||Phil||09-10-2001||12:47 PM||||The "hoods"( the one in front over the spare tire) are all the same- the "trunks"( in the back over the engine) are differrent, GT vs. notchback||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-10-2001||12:59 PM||||There are two types of side molding. Rounded and "grooved". If your car is a "fastback" GT, meaning 86 or later, it has the round molding. The only notchbacks that have the round molding are the 87 base coupe (NOT the SE) and the 88 coupe and Formula. <BR>Side marker lights are interchangeable, as long as they are from a car with the same type of molding as yours.<BR>If your GT is an 85, it has the grooved molding. This is the same molding that's on the Indy, all SE's, and all base coupes before 87.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
